The learning mode was broken after commit 8afd3bd - when the countdown timer expired, it would show the answer but fail to automatically advance to the next item, causing the session to pause unexpectedly.

## Problem
In the `startCountdown` function, when the countdown reached zero, the code called `showAnswer()` and `resetProgressBar()` regardless of whether the user was in learning mode or training mode. This caused learning mode to behave like training mode - showing the answer but then pausing instead of continuing automatically.

## Solution
Modified the countdown expiration logic in `src/js/game/play.js` to differentiate between the two modes:

- **Learning mode**: Calls `nextItem(true)` to auto-advance with vibration feedback
- **Training mode**: Calls `showAnswer()` and `resetProgressBar()` to show answer and pause for manual advancement

```javascript
if (gameState.isLearningMode) {
  // In learning mode, auto-advance to next item with vibration
  nextItem(true);
} else {
  // In training mode, just show the answer and pause
  showAnswer();
  resetProgressBar();
}
```

## Testing
- ✅ Learning mode now auto-advances continuously with proper timing intervals
- ✅ Vibration feedback works correctly for auto-advance notifications  
- ✅ Training mode preserves existing behavior (shows answer then pauses)
- ✅ All existing functionality remains intact

![Training mode after countdown](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4aca47fa-9288-4d13-b56d-5c5d34a32b99)

*Training mode correctly shows the answer and pauses after countdown expires, while learning mode (not shown) automatically advances to the next item.*

Fixes #48.

